    <grid>
      <Value><![CDATA[{
  "name": "1 column layout",
  "sections": [
    {
      "grid": "12",
      "rows": [
        {
          "name": "Article Full",
          "id": "309e2d4b-2d7d-4f87-ba89-b73f65ff57bf",
          "areas": [
            {
              "grid": "12",
              "controls": [
                {
                  "value": "<p><em>SANRAL begins major roadworks by upgrading a 6.4km stretch between Cato Ridge and Pietermaritzburg.Test <br></em></p>",
                  "editor": {
                    "alias": "rte",
                    "view": "rte"
                  },
                  "styles": null,
                  "config": null
                },
                {
                  "value": {
                    "focalPoint": {
                      "left": 0.5,
                      "top": 0.5
                    },
                    "id": 1767,
                    "udi": "umb://media/45493330b0c146d2aecb910c794bb29c",
                    "image": "/media/gyzfsrob/untitled-2.jpg"
                  },
                  "editor": {
                    "alias": "media",
                    "view": "media"
                  },
                  "styles": null,
                  "config": null
                },
                {
                  "value": "<p> </p>\n<p>Over the next 48 months SANRAL will be upgrading the four-lane dual carriageway road between Cato Ridge and Pietermaritzburg to an eight-lane dual carriageway.</p>\n<p>This 6.4km stretch of road begins at the Dardanelles interchange and ends at the Lynnfield Park interchange. The existing Dardanelles interchange will also be upgraded to improve traffic flow.</p>\n<p>Roadlab has been contracted as the site materials laboratory for this 4-year project, which SANRAL projects will create 700 employment opportunities.</p>\n<p>After these critical sections between Cato Ridge and Pietermaritzburg, SANRAL's focus will shift to the Key Ridge realignment and the EB Cloete to Paradise Valley section.</p>\n<p>This N3 upgrade will include the construction of South Africa's first network arch bridge, creating space for additional lanes without any support piers.</p>\n<p>You can see all of the major upgrades planned for the N3 by SANRAL below, courtesy of <a href=\"https://businesstech.co.za/news/motoring/468616/one-of-south-africas-busiest-highways-is-getting-an-upgrade-including-a-new-r300-million-bridge/\">Business Tech</a>.</p>\n<p> </p>",
                  "editor": {
                    "alias": "rte",
                    "view": "rte"
                  },
                  "styles": null,
                  "config": null
                },
                {
                  "value": {
                    "constrain": true,
                    "height": 240,
                    "width": 360,
                    "url": "https://twitter.com/MbalulaFikile/status/1361622492050313216?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw%7Ctwcamp%5Etweetembed%7Ctwterm%5E1361622492050313216%7Ctwgr%5E%7Ctwcon%5Es1_&ref_url=https%3A%2F%2Fbusinesstech.co.za%2Fnews%2Fmotoring%2F468616%2Fone-of-south-africas-busiest-highways-is-getting-an-upgrade-including-a-new-r300-million-bridge%2F",
                    "info": "",
                    "preview": "<blockquote class=\"twitter-tweet\" data-width=\"360\"><p lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\">The N3 upgrade project will improve the capacity of the N3 from the Westville Viaduct to the Paradise Valley Interchange in KwaZulu-Natal. The total length of construction will be a massive 1 666km and will include an innovative arch bridge to span the N3. <a href=\"https://t.co/uPxQqzSpH2\">pic.twitter.com/uPxQqzSpH2</a></p>&mdash; |Mr Fix (@MbalulaFikile) <a href=\"https://twitter.com/MbalulaFikile/status/1361622492050313216?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw\">February 16, 2021</a></blockquote>\n<script async src=\"https://platform.twitter.com/widgets.js\" charset=\"utf-8\"></script>\n"
                  },
                  "editor": {
                    "alias": "embed",
                    "view": "embed"
                  },
